      "description": "The IRIS skills: `iris-dspace` (how IRIS uses DSpace and qualified Dublin Core, stated as checkable requirements R1–R22), `iris-rest-feed`, `iris-cdn-exporter`, `iris-cdn-signing` and `iris-oxigraph`; and, under `voices/`, the WHO style guide's three house voices, declared from within by `skills.json`. Kept thin: the Dublin Core type lives in folio-assistant-core, enumeration and subsetting in large-datasets, and OCR is a cat-harness platform tool.",
